Build a backend application using FastAPI and SQLite that implements full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for two related tables connected via a Foreign Key (FK) relationship.

Core Requirements
Database & ORM:

Use SQLite as the database.

Use SQLAlchemy to define the database tables and relationships.

Establish a One-to-Many relationship between two entities of your choice (e.g., Category and Product, or Author and Book).

Data Validation:

Use Pydantic schemas for request body validation, response serialization, and handling foreign key associations.

Required Endpoints:

Parent Entity CRUD:

Create a parent record.

Read all parent records (including their associated child records).

Read a single parent record by ID.

Delete a parent record (with cascade delete for related child records).

Child Entity CRUD (Foreign Key Dependent):

Create a child record linked specifically to an existing parent ID.

Read all child records.

Delete a child record by ID.

Deliverables:

A modular project file structure (database.py, models.py, schemas.py, main.py).

Fully working endpoints testable through FastAPI's automatic interactive documentation (/docs).